---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---

<BaseLayout title="Digital Signage System – Bryce Kennedy">
    <article class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 pt-40 pb-16 md:pt-44 md:pb-20">
        <!-- Back Navigation -->
        <a
            href="../"
            class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 text-sm text-slate-300 hover:text-brand-orange transition-colors mb-8"
        >
            <svg
                xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
                width="16"
                height="16"
                viewBox="0 0 24 24"
                fill="none"
                stroke="currentColor"
                stroke-width="2"
                stroke-linecap="round"
                stroke-linejoin="round"
            >
                <path d="m15 18-6-6 6-6"></path>
            </svg>
            Back to projects
        </a>

        <!-- Project Header -->
        <header class="space-y-4 mb-12">
            <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-3 mb-4">
                <div class="flex flex-col items-center gap-1">
                    <div
                        class="p-2 rounded-full border border-gray-dark/70 bg-surface-card"
                    >
                        <img
                            src={`${base}icons/wordpress-svgrepo-com.svg`}
                            alt=""
                            class="w-5 h-5 brightness-0 invert"
                        />
                    </div>
                    <span class="text-[10px] text-slate-400">WordPress</span>
                </div>
                <div class="flex flex-col items-center gap-1">
                    <div
                        class="p-2 rounded-full border border-gray-dark/70 bg-surface-card"
                    >
                        <img
                            src={`${base}icons/typescript-svgrepo-com.svg`}
                            alt=""
                            class="w-5 h-5 brightness-0 invert"
                        />
                    </div>
                    <span class="text-[10px] text-slate-400">TypeScript</span>
                </div>
                <div class="flex flex-col items-center gap-1">
                    <div
                        class="p-2 rounded-full border border-gray-dark/70 bg-surface-card"
                    >
                        <img
                            src={`${base}icons/javascript-svgrepo-com.svg`}
                            alt=""
                            class="w-5 h-5 brightness-0 invert"
                        />
                    </div>
                    <span class="text-[10px] text-slate-400">JavaScript</span>
                </div>
                <div class="flex flex-col items-center gap-1">
                    <div
                        class="p-2 rounded-full border border-gray-dark/70 bg-surface-card"
                    >
                        <img
                            src={`${base}icons/html5-01-svgrepo-com.svg`}
                            alt=""
                            class="w-5 h-5 brightness-0 invert"
                        />
                    </div>
                    <span class="text-[10px] text-slate-400">HTML</span>
                </div>
                <div class="flex flex-col items-center gap-1">
                    <div
                        class="p-2 rounded-full border border-gray-dark/70 bg-surface-card"
                    >
                        <img
                            src={`${base}icons/css3-01-svgrepo-com.svg`}
                            alt=""
                            class="w-5 h-5 brightness-0 invert"
                        />
                    </div>
                    <span class="text-[10px] text-slate-400">CSS</span>
                </div>
            </div>

            <h1 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-semibold">
                Digital Signage System
            </h1>

            <div class="aspect-video bg-gray-dark/30 overflow-hidden">
                <video
                    autoplay
                    loop
                    muted
                    playsinline
                    class="w-full h-full object-cover group-hover:scale-105 transition-transform duration-300"
                >
                    <source
                        src={`${base}videos/digital-signage-intro.mp4`}
                        type="video/mp4"
                    />
                </video>
            </div>

            <p class="text-lg text-slate-300">
                Built and maintained a high-visibility digital signage platform
                serving thousands of displays across the enterprise.
            </p>
        </header>

        <!-- Project Content -->
        <div
            class="prose prose-invert prose-slate mx-auto max-w-3xl space-y-8 leading-relaxed text-lg"
        >
            <section
                id="case-digital-signage"
                class="case case-section first:mt-0 first:pt-0 first:border-t-0 pt-8 mt-8 border-t border-gray-dark/20 space-y-4"
            >
                <header class="case-header mb-4">
                    <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-3">
                        Digital Signage CMS for American Airlines
                    </h2>

                    <p class="case-summary mb-4">
                        As part of American Airlines’ new corporate campus
                        initiative, I designed and built a <strong
                            >custom digital signage content management system</strong
                        > to power a network of <strong>100+ screens</strong> and
                        <strong>six large-format LED displays</strong>
                        across multiple buildings and global offices. Off-the-shelf
                        signage platforms couldn’t meet the need for <strong
                            >creative flexibility</strong
                        >,
                        <strong>real-time data integration</strong>, and <strong
                            >centralized control</strong
                        >—so I built one from the ground up. Using a <strong
                            >heavily customized WordPress foundation</strong
                        >, the platform lets Corporate Communications schedule,
                        manage, and animate content seamlessly across
                        devices—from small embedded screens to massive LED
                        walls— supporting <strong>HD video</strong>, <strong
                            >live API-driven data feeds</strong
                        >, and
                        <strong>continuous 24/7 playback</strong> with strict brand
                        consistency and performance optimization.
                    </p>

                    <figure class="my-8">
                        <div
                            class="aspect-video bg-gray-dark/30 overflow-hidden rounded"
                        >
                            <video
                                autoplay
                                loop
                                muted
                                playsinline
                                class="w-full h-full object-cover"
                            >
                                <source
                                    src={`${base}videos/digital-signage-vis-01.mp4`}
                                    type="video/mp4"
                                />
                            </video>
                        </div>
                        <figcaption class="mt-3 text-sm text-slate-400">
                            <strong
                                >Live data visualizations on large-format
                                displays.</strong
                            >
                            Real-time operational and performance data streamed from
                            internal APIs and rendered as readable, animated visualizations—designed
                            to remain legible and meaningful even at architectural
                            scale.
                        </figcaption>
                    </figure>
                </header>

                <section
                    id="overview"
                    class="case-section pt-8 mt-8 border-t border-gray-dark/20 space-y-4"
                >
                    <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-3">Overview</h3>
                    <p class="mb-4">
                        The campus deployment combined high-impact LED walls
                        with a wide network of smaller information screens. The
                        goal was to deliver immersive multimedia, real-time
                        updates, and location-relevant communications while
                        maintaining a cohesive visual language and reliable,
                        always-on performance.
                    </p>
                    <p class="mb-4">
                        The end result was a purpose-built CMS and delivery
                        pipeline optimized for diverse hardware
                        profiles—designed so non-technical editors could launch
                        and manage content confidently without engineering
                        involvement.
                    </p>
                </section>

                <section
                    id="requirements-and-challenges"
                    class="case-section pt-8 mt-8 border-t border-gray-dark/20 space-y-4"
                >
                    <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-3">
                        Requirements &amp; Challenges
                    </h3>

                    <p class="mb-4">
                        When American Airlines opened its new corporate campus,
                        it created an opportunity to reimagine employee
                        engagement through real-time data, immersive multimedia,
                        and large-scale digital experiences. The buildings were
                        equipped with a network of information screens and
                        several large-format LED displays—high-impact visual
                        canvases designed to bring culture and communications to
                        life.
                    </p>

                    <figure class="my-8">
                        <div
                            class="aspect-video bg-gray-dark/30 overflow-hidden rounded"
                        >
                            <video
                                autoplay
                                loop
                                muted
                                playsinline
                                class="w-full h-full object-cover"
                            >
                                <source
                                    src={`${base}videos/digital-display-monitors-01.mp4`}
                                    type="video/mp4"
                                />
                            </video>
                        </div>
                        <figcaption class="mt-3 text-sm text-slate-400">
                            <strong
                                >Adaptive data presentation on embedded
                                displays.</strong
                            >
                            The same real-time data feeds were reflowed and optimized
                            for lower-power embedded devices, preserving clarity and
                            performance while adapting layouts, animation density,
                            and refresh behavior.
                        </figcaption>
                    </figure>

                    <p class="mb-4">
                        The Corporate Communications team needed a centralized
                        system to
                        <strong>control, curate, and schedule content</strong> across
                        this growing ecosystem. Existing signage products offered
                        useful features, but not the level of
                        <strong
                            >customization, scalability, and creative
                            flexibility</strong
                        > required. A
                        <strong>bespoke CMS</strong> was necessary—capable of managing
                        hundreds of displays, accommodating diverse hardware, and
                        delivering dynamic, brand-consistent content 24/7.
                    </p>

                    <h4 class="text-lg font-semibold mt-6 mb-2">
                        Key challenges
                    </h4>
                    <ul class="list-none space-y-3 mb-4 pl-0 ml-0">
                        <li>
                            <strong>Centralized control at scale:</strong> One system
                            to manage campaigns, schedules, and updates across many
                            screens and locations.
                        </li>
                        <li>
                            <strong>Hardware diversity:</strong> High-performance
                            PCs for LED walls vs. lightweight embedded devices for
                            smaller displays—requiring different delivery strategies.
                        </li>
                        <li>
                            <strong>Always-on reliability:</strong> Continuous 24/7
                            playback with smooth transitions between video, animation,
                            and live data.
                        </li>
                        <li>
                            <strong
                                >Creative flexibility with brand safety:</strong
                            > Motion and layout needed to feel dynamic while staying
                            consistent and brand-correct.
                        </li>
                    </ul>

                    <p class="mb-4">
                        Six large-format LED displays—each roughly the size of a
                        shipping container
                        <!-- TODO: insert exact dimensions here, e.g., 9.6m × 2.7m -->
                        —were installed across the campus, including a centerpiece
                        at the main entrance. These displays welcome visitors and
                        keep employees informed with motion graphics, streaming video,
                        and real-time data visualizations. They needed to operate
                        continuously and transition smoothly between media types while
                        maintaining brand fidelity.
                    </p>

                    <figure class="my-8">
                        <div class="bg-gray-dark/30 overflow-hidden rounded">
                            <video
                                autoplay
                                loop
                                muted
                                playsinline
                                class="w-full h-full object-cover"
                            >
                                <source
                                    src={`${base}videos/digital-display-transition-01.mp4`}
                                    type="video/mp4"
                                />
                            </video>
                        </div>
                        <figcaption class="mt-3 text-sm text-slate-400">
                            <strong
                                >Brand-safe motion across large-format LED
                                walls.</strong
                            >
                            Smooth, hardware-aware transitions between full-screen
                            video, motion graphics, and live content ensured visual
                            continuity across massive LED displays—without dropped
                            frames or visible tearing during 24/7 playback.
                        </figcaption>
                    </figure>

                    <p class="mb-4">
                        Beyond the headline displays, a network of <strong
                            >100+ smaller screens</strong
                        > was deployed throughout the campus <!-- TODO: insert exact sizes here -->,
                        with hundreds more in hubs and offices worldwide. These
                        localized screens deliver real-time updates, performance
                        metrics, and employee communications tailored to each
                        location. Hardware diversity was a major
                        challenge—demanding a <strong
                            >dual-architecture approach</strong
                        >
                        to preserve visual quality and frame pacing across environments.
                    </p>
                </section>
            </section>
        </div>
    </article>
</BaseLayout>
